}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" 13194139539104 17592186576411 false] [17592186530418 1074 "To compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to each component of $w.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, with $$\n\\displaystyle x={[\\begin{aligned}5,\\,3\\end{aligned}]}^{T},\n$$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 true] [17592186530418 1074 "To compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to each component of $w.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, with $x={[\\begin{aligned}5,\\,3\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 false] [17592186530419 1071 "Find the general solution to the matrix differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\,{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 true] [17592186530419 1071 "Find the general solution to the matrix differential equation $\\,{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]x(t).$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 false] [17592186530421 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at $$\n\\displaystyle {x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 true] [17592186530421 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 false] [17592186530421 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at $$\n\\displaystyle {x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}({x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}0+3(2) & 1+2 & 3(1)+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 true] [17592186530421 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}({x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}0+3(2) & 1+2 & 3(1)+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539104 17592186576411 false] [17592186530430 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(x)$ where $$\n\\displaystyle x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\